Rocks'n'Diamonds @VERSION@ for AmigaOS 3.x (AmiCradle)
==============================================================

Rocks'n'Diamonds is Holger Schemel's arcade puzzle game in the line of
Boulder Dash, Emerald Mine, Supaplex and Sokoban: dig through the earth,
collect the gems, mind the falling rocks and the creatures, and reach the
exit. It has a level editor and a tape recorder that saves and replays
games. This is its AmigaOS 3.x build for a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, with
SDL 2, SDL2_image and SDL2_mixer through GFOpenGPU. Status: TESTING.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.2, a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, AmiCradle or an RTG board
  with an 800x600 (or larger) screen mode.
- GFOpenGPU with SDL2.module, SDL2_image.module and SDL2_mixer.module, in
  LIBS:GFOpenGPU/ or in the older LIBS:OpenGPU/ (the Installer copies them
  across).
- AHI for sound. GFOpenInput for pads (lowlevel.library alone gives the
  joystick port).
- About 6 MB on disk.

Installing
----------

1. Unpack the archive somewhere other than where the game will go, for
   example to RAM:, with OpenCompress (AmigaOS 3.2 has no lha command):
     OpenCompress x rocksndiamonds-@VERSION@-68040.lha RAM:
2. Open RAM: and double-click Install-RocksnDiamonds.
3. Choose where the RocksnDiamonds drawer goes (Work:Games by default).

The Installer checks the Installer version and the processor, copies the
drawer and its icon, and copies any SDL module that is only in
LIBS:OpenGPU/ to LIBS:GFOpenGPU/. Run it again to update the game: your
players, settings, saved games and own levels are kept.

Playing
-------

- Double-click the game's icon, or from a Shell: cd to the drawer, then
  rocksndiamonds. It loads its graphics for a minute or two, then shows its
  menu on an 800x600 screen of its own. F11 or Alt+Return switches to a
  window on the Workbench and back.
- The cursor keys move; Left Ctrl with a direction snaps (digs or collects
  without moving); Right Ctrl places dynamite; Space pauses; Escape leaves
  a game. Return chooses in the menus.
- F1 saves the game you are playing (on the tape), F2 loads it again.
- A joystick or pad in port 2 also moves player 1: the first button snaps.
- The level sets are the three tutorials (Niko Boehm's, Aaron Davidson's
  and ncrecc's). More level sets from the Rocks'n'Diamonds web site can be
  unpacked into the drawer userdata/levels.
- Everything the game writes is in the drawer userdata (made on the first
  start): players, settings, saved games, scores, your own levels.
- There is no network play in this build.

Licence
-------

Rocks'n'Diamonds is GPL-2.0 (COPYING in the drawer), (c) 1995-2026 Holger
Schemel, Artsoft Entertainment; its source is at
https://github.com/ArtsoftEntertainment/rocksndiamonds. The game's own
data in this drawer (graphics, sounds, the rhythm loop, the tutorial level
sets, the help texts) is upstream's own and is shipped under the same
GPL-2.0 terms that upstream's and Arch Linux's packages give it; Debian
treats its licence as unclear. The classic level sets of the original
games and the three music modules from upstream's tree are not included.
The credits are in docs/credits.

